w energy from the Sun  just like plants do through  photosynthesis  Bulbasaur can extend long and powerful  vines from the bulb on its back and use  them as both a weapon and a tool for  accomplishing various tasks when it  comes time for a Bulbasaur to evolve its  body will light up in a glory  blue color and it evolves into Ivysaur  at level 16 and into Venusaur at level  32 penis or still looks a lot like  bulbasaur except that it is bigger and a  bulb on its back sprouts into a large  red flower Bulbasaur is weak against  certain types of Pokemon like fire and  flying but he is strong against other  types like water Bulbasaur has the  highest base stat total out of all the  starters with 318 compared to squirrels  314 and charmander's 309 although he is  believed to be the least popular out of  the three primary starters many have  argued that Bulbasaur is statistically  the best choice out of the three I will  leave a link to a video that argues that  exact point in the description below  Bulbasaur's japanese name is Fushigi  denis and that's it for the Kanto region  starters now moving on to Johto  wait I feel like I'm forgetting  something yes of course in the Kanto  region we also have Pikachu Pikachu is  an electric-type pokémon that is the  only available starter in pokemon yellow  Pikachu is essentially a yellow electric  Mouse who can alternate between walking  on two feet and on all fours it stores  electricity in the pouches inside its  cheeks as a way for the player to mirror  the journey that Ash goes on in the  first season of the anime pokemon yellow  makes Pikachu your only available  starter and then it gives you a chance  to catch the other three starters  through special events that are not  available in the previous games normally  a Pikachu will evolve into right you  through the use of a thunder stone but  just like Ash's Pikachu your starter in  pokemon yellow will refuse to evolve so  the only way to evolve it is to trade it  first  Pichu 