 the heaviest and tallest out  of all the water type starters and its  name appears to be a combination of the  words taught as in small child or  toddler and crocodiles so he is  basically a baby crocodile Totodile  evolves into Kraken ah at level 18 and  into Feraligatr at level 30  Totodile is weak to grass and  electric-type pokémon but strong against  fire steel and ice types it's total base  stats are 314 so 5 higher than cyndaquil  and it's Japanese name  is one in O club and finally we have  chikorita the grass type starter of the  johto region chikorita is a small green  creature that walks on 4 legs and has a  leaf growing out of the top of its head  like Bulbasaur chikorita also has the  ability to use vines that come in handy  as either tools or weapons and  unsurprisingly in the wild Chikorita is  liked to hang out in grassy areas  chikorita evolves into bayleaf at level  16 and into Meganium at level 32 it has  a base stats total of 318 which is  higher than both cyndaquil and Totodile  nonetheless Chikorita has quite a few  weaknesses including fire poison ice bug  and flying-type pokémon it is strong  against water electric and ground types  as well as other grass type Pokemon  Chikorita was initially designed with a  yellow body but this was later changed  to green it's Japanese name is also  Chikorita and in fact Chiquita's  evolutions bay leaf and Meganium also  have the same names in English and  Japanese and now on to the Hoenn region  Torchic is the fire type starter pokémon  in the Hoenn region Torchic is basically  the fried chicken Pokemon since Torchic  is a baby chicken that keeps an internal  flame somewhere inside its stomach  Torchic is capable of using fire type  attacks that can reach temperatures of  up to 1,000 degrees Celsius  rather than mountains or volcanoes  Torchic is a fire-type Pokemon that  tends to inhabit grassy areas in the  wild torchic's name is a combination of  the words torch and chick meaning baby  chicken it evolves into a Combusken at  level 16 and into Blaziken at level 36  tor tricks japanese name is accommo and  its base stats total is 310 it is weak  against water ground and rock types but  strong against grass I steel plug fairy  and other fire type Pokemon Torchic  weighs the least out of all the fire  type starter Pokemon next up is Mudkip  the water type starter pokémon in the  Hoenn region Mudkip is amphibious  meaning that it can live on both land  and water and in the wild it can be  found in swamps and martial  for that reason it is known as the mud  fish pokémon Mudkip can actually use the  fin on its head to sense changes in  water and air currents giving it a  strong sense of spatial awareness Mudkip  has a base that's total of 310 just like  Torchic it is weak against electric and  grass type Pokemon which makes sense for  a water type and it is strong against  fire steel and ice Mudkip evolves into  Marshtomp at level 16 and Swampert at  level 36 its english name Mudkip is  essentially a combination of the words  mud and skip and it's Japanese name is  Mizumoto there is actually an amphibious  fish in the real world known as the  mudskipper and this animal was likely  the inspiration for Mudkip and the grass  type starter in the Hoenn region is  Treecko Treecko is essentially a green  lizard who walks on two feet and as he  is the wood gecko pokémon we know that  he was inspired by the real-life gecko  like many lizards Treecko is an  extremely skilled climber and in the  wild Treecko can be found in large  forests and tall trees treecko's long  tail allows it to sense environmental  factors like humidity enabling it to  predict the weather for the next day  just like the other two Hoenn starters  treecko's base stats total is 310 he  evolves into Grovyle at level 16 and  Sceptile at level 36 Treecko is weak to  quite a few Pokemon types including fire  flying poison bug and ice he is strong  against water Electric ground and other  grass types treecko's En